---
import { bounds, story } from "../../lib/coverage";
import { noScore, pipeline, rileyAsk, spell, toPlay } from "../../lib/cases";
import KickThink from "./KickThink.astro";
import PartHead from "./PartHead.astro";
import NextPart from "./NextPart.astro";
import AiStudy from "./AiStudy.astro";
import { donePrompt } from "../../lib/primer";

const rewindThoughts = [
  "Riley asked me to list every expected page and match before collecting, and to name every gap in the summary—so I can't just count what gets saved and call it done.",
  `Expected set: ${pipeline.asked} school schedule pages and ${story.scheduled} scheduled conference matches (${story.schools} × ${story.schools - 1}), minus ${spell(toPlay)} still to play—so ${story.finals} finished matches to account for.`,
  `Dunmore's schedule timed out after three tries. If I only read each match from the host's page, I'll drop ${spell(bounds.unseen)} Dunmore home matches—let me recover those from the visitors' saved pages instead.`,
  `That counts ${story.afterRepair} of ${story.finals}. ${noScore.home} vs. ${noScore.away} on ${noScore.day} is marked final with no score on either schedule, and its box score page wasn't requested yet. I'll leave it uncounted and name both gaps in the record.`,
];

const record = [
  ["Schedule pages", `${pipeline.asked} expected, ${pipeline.saved} saved. Dunmore: unavailable, no answer after three tries.`],
  ["Matches", `${story.scheduled} scheduled by the format, ${toPlay} still to play, ${story.finals} finished.`],
  ["Counted", `${story.counted} from the hosts' pages. ${spell(bounds.unseen, true)} Dunmore home matches from the visitors' saved pages.`],
  ["Not counted", `${noScore.home} vs. ${noScore.away}, ${noScore.day}: final, no score on either schedule. Box score page not requested yet.`],
];
---

<section id="rewind">
  <PartHead id="rewind">Rewind: Friday with a coverage requirement</PartHead>
  <p>Here is Riley's original prompt again:</p>
  <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's original prompt">
    <div class="cv-chat-bar">
      <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
      <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick</span>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-chat-text">{rileyAsk}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-commit" data-commit>
    <p class="cv-kind">Write it <span>you check your own</span></p>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-added">Add the one sentence that was missing.</label>
    <textarea id="cv-added" rows="2" placeholder="What would you require Kick to report?" data-save="added"></textarea>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button type="button" data-commit-btn disabled>Compare and replay Friday</button>
      <button type="button" class="cv-link-btn" data-commit-skip>Skip and show example</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a short sentence to compare, or skip ahead.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p class="cv-model">Before you collect, list every school schedule page and every finished match the conference format says the table should include. In your summary, report what happened to each one, and name every gap and why.</p>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Check what yours covers:</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-set" /><span>Lists what should be collected before the run starts, from the schools and the format</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-each" /><span>Reports what happened to each expected page and match</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-gaps" /><span>Requires the summary to name every gap and why</span></label>
      </fieldset>

      <h3>What Kick returns when asked</h3>
      <p class="cv-label">Simulated response. Same agent, same Dunmore outage.</p>
      <KickThink duration="Thought for 8s" thoughts={rewindThoughts} />
      <div class="cv-agent-reply" role="region" aria-label="Kick's coverage record">
        <div class="cv-chat-bar">
          <span class="cv-agent-badge">Kick · Coding agent</span>
          <span class="cv-status-note">{story.afterRepair} of {story.finals} · gaps named</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-agent-record">
          <table class="cv-log cv-record">
            <caption>Kick's coverage record, Friday</caption>
            <tbody>{record.map(([what, said]) => <tr><th scope="row">{what}</th><td>{said}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-say">
        <p class="cv-who">Riley, to the eight schools <span>Friday afternoon</span></p>
        <p>Conference table attached. Through Friday, it counts {story.afterRepair} of {story.finals} finished conference matches. Dunmore's page did not answer, so its {spell(bounds.unseen)} home results come from the visitors' pages. {noScore.home} vs. {noScore.away} on {noScore.day} is final with no score on either schedule. Its box score page has not been requested yet, so both schools are one match short.</p>
      </div>
      <p>The outage didn't disappear. In the original run, Kick counted {story.counted} of {story.finals} finished matches. Once the expected set was written down, {spell(bounds.unseen)} of the {spell(story.finals - story.counted)} missing matches showed up as Dunmore home matches, so Kick recovered them from the visitors' saved schedules.</p>
      <p class="cv-rule">All {story.finals} finished matches are accounted for: {story.counted} counted from the hosts' pages, {bounds.unseen} from the visitors' saved pages, and one named and not counted.</p>
      <p>The extra sentence did not fix Friday on its own. It set <strong>acceptance criteria</strong>: conditions Kick's work had to meet before Riley would accept it. Meeting them produced a coverage record, and Riley checked that record before publishing: {spell(pipeline.asked)} pages expected, every gap named, and the {spell(bounds.unseen)} recovered results traced to the visitors' saved pages.</p>
      <div class="cv-say cv-yours" data-close-first hidden>
        <p class="cv-who">Your question from Publish Day</p>
        <p><q></q> Would its answer have surfaced Dunmore's missing page?</p>
      </div>
      <AiStudy
        id="rewind-ai-study"
        title="Giving an agent acceptance criteria"
        note="Send this prompt to read the reply an AI assistant gave, or copy it into your own. Then come back and check Kick's record against the expected set."
        prompt={donePrompt}
        href="../01-collection-ai-done/"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
  <NextPart from="rewind">If nobody had called, how would you spot a missing match?</NextPart>
</section>
